 "about": "Front PT0: the pt-BR glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-pt-br.md §3.2–3.3) that src/i18n/pt-br/pt-br.test.ts enforces through the SC4 lint framework (src/i18n/lint/, profile pt-BR) on every Portuguese string. Seeded from the Spanish glossary: the same English patterns and interface names, re-targeted to Portuguese from the English (Spanish only as meaning context) and the IAU Office of Astronomy for Education pt-BR glossary. A term applies when its English pattern matches the English source: the Portuguese must then match the `pt` stem or pattern. Names are fixed interface names (an exact name applies only to a whole string). Forbidden here are the term forms this glossary rejects; the language-wide rules (European-Portuguese words, spellings and accents, «estar a» + infinitive, tu-forms where você is decided, Spanish words left from the Spanish reference, claims that a translation is CLEA's or official) live in the pt-BR profile of src/i18n/lint/profiles.ts. Rows for areas still in English wait for their sub-front (PT1–PT6). Translations are web adaptations by OpenVireo, never CLEA's.",
